BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sub60-2026-w15d2@training.local
DTSTAMP:20261124T161800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261124
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261125
SUMMARY:W15D2 | Bike 75m + Run/Walk 24m
DESCRIPTION:W15D2 | Base → Build transition\nPlanned training: 99 min (ex
 cluding extra walking warm-up).\n\nBIKE — 75 min\n10 min Z1 warm-up\n25 
 min Z2\n15 min Z2 at 80–85 rpm\n15 min Z2\n10 min Z1 cool-down\nRPE 3–
 4\, conversational. No unverified FTP targets. Do not force left/right bal
 ance.\n\nRUN/WALK — 24 min\n3 × (5 min easy run + 3 min walk)\n15 min r
 unning\, 9 min walking.\nWalk a few minutes before starting (extra time). 
 Flat route\, RPE 2–3. Stop for local pain.\n\nCALF CHECK\nDo not run if 
 symptoms persist from the previous session. Stop for local pain. If tightn
 ess resolves by next day\, do not increase load. Persistent symptoms: skip
  next run. Walking pain or focal bone tenderness: pause running and seek s
 ports medicine evaluation.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sub60-2026-w15d3@training.local
DTSTAMP:20261124T161800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261125
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261126
SUMMARY:W15D3 | SWIM CSS TEST — 1700 yd
DESCRIPTION:W15D3 | Base → Build transition\nPlanned training: 60 min (ex
 cluding extra walking warm-up).\n\nSWIM — CSS TEST — 1700 yd / 60 min\
 n25 yd pool. No equipment throughout. No dive start. Use consistent turns.
 \n\n1. 400 yd easy warm-up\; rest 30s.\n2. 4 × 50 yd progressive\; rest 2
 0s after each.\n3. 4 × 25 yd fast\, not all-out\; rest 30s after each.\n4
 . 400 yd timed maximum sustainable effort. Start controlled\, maintain pac
 e\, finish hard.\n5. 200 yd very easy recovery\; then rest poolside so tot
 al recovery between tests is about 10 min.\n6. 200 yd timed maximum sustai
 nable effort\; finish last 50 yd hard. Rest 60s.\n7. 200 yd easy cool-down
 .\n\nRECORD\n400 yd time and 100 yd splits\; 200 yd time and 50 yd splits\
 ; strokes/length\, stroke rate\, SWOLF\, RPE and calf symptoms.\nCSS (seco
 nds/100 yd) = (400 yd seconds − 200 yd seconds)/2.\nCurrent recorded CSS
 : 1:52/100 yd until updated by valid test.\nStop if wall push-off causes c
 alf pain.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sub60-2026-w15d4@training.local
DTSTAMP:20261124T161800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261126
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261127
SUMMARY:W15D4 | Bike 90m + Strength 25m
DESCRIPTION:W15D4 | Base → Build transition\nPlanned training: 115 min (e
 xcluding extra walking warm-up).\n\nBIKE — 90 min\n10 min Z1 warm-up\n30
  min Z2\n5 min Z1\n30 min Z2\n5 min low Z2\n10 min Z1 cool-down\n80–90 r
 pm\, seated. No threshold or Sweet Spot.\n\nSTRENGTH — 25 min\nGlute bri
 dge: 2 × 15\; rest 45s.\nBodyweight squat: 2 × 12\; rest 60s.\nSide-lyin
 g hip abduction: 2 × 12/side\; rest 30s.\nDead bug: 2 × 10/side\; rest 3
 0s.\nSide plank: 2 × 30s/side\; rest 30s.\nSeated calf isometric: 3 × 30
 s\; rest 30s\; only if painless and consistent with PT guidance.\nNo failu
 re\, jumping or heavy eccentric work.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sub60-2026-w15d5@training.local
DTSTAMP:20261124T161800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261127
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261128
SUMMARY:W15D5 | Swim 2600 yd + Run/Walk 24m
DESCRIPTION:W15D5 | Base → Build transition\nPlanned training: 84 min (ex
 cluding extra walking warm-up).\n\nSWIM — 2600 yd / 60 min (estimated)\n
 25 yd pool. Rest after each repeat as listed.\n\n1. 400 yd easy\, RPE 3\; 
 no equipment\; rest 30s.\n2. 2 × 50 yd: first 25 catch awareness\, second
  25 normal swim\; pull buoy\; rest 20s.\n3. 2 × 50 yd body balance and ca
 tch\; no equipment\; rest 20s.\n4. 400 yd steady aerobic\, RPE 4–5\; no 
 equipment\; rest 30s.\n5. 400 yd body position and rhythm\; pull buoy\; re
 st 30s.\n6. 400 yd maintain first-repeat efficiency\; no equipment\; rest 
 45s.\n7. 2 × 100 yd steady catch\, RPE 4\; small paddles + pull buoy\; re
 st 20s.\n8. 4 × 100 yd transfer catch sensation\; no equipment\; rest 20s
 .\n9. 200 yd easy cool-down\; no equipment.\n\nPACE: unassisted 400s = new
  CSS + 8–15s/100 yd\; unassisted 100s = CSS + 5–10s/100 yd. Assisted s
 ets by RPE. If no valid new CSS\, use RPE. Record 400s separately. No fins
  or dedicated kicking.\n\nRUN/WALK — 24 min\n3 × (5 min easy run + 3 mi
 n walk). Run 15 min total. Extra walking warm-up. Flat route\, RPE 2–3. 
 No progression or fast brick.\n\nCALF CHECK\nDo not run if symptoms persis
 t from the previous session. Stop for local pain. If tightness resolves by
  next day\, do not increase load. Persistent symptoms: skip next run. Walk
 ing pain or focal bone tenderness: pause running and seek sports medicine 
 evaluation.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sub60-2026-w15d6@training.local
DTSTAMP:20261124T161800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261128
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261129
SUMMARY:W15D6 | BIKE FTP TEST — 75m
DESCRIPTION:W15D6 | Base → Build transition\nPlanned training: 75 min (ex
 cluding extra walking warm-up).\n\nBIKE — FTP TEST — 75 min\nCAAD12 + 
 Magene P715S. Zero-offset calibration. Prefer stable\, ventilated indoor s
 etup\; ERG off. Record power\, HR\, cadence and L/R balance.\n\n1. 20 min 
 warm-up\, Z1 progressing to Z2.\n2. 6 min: 3 × (1 min fast cadence + 1 mi
 n easy).\n3. 5 min hard\, near maximum sustainable 5-min power.\n4. 10 min
  very easy recovery.\n5. 20 min timed maximum sustainable average power.\n
    0–5 min: controlled\, RPE 7–8.\n   5–10 min: steady\, RPE 8–9.\
 n   10–15 min: maintain\, RPE 9.\n   15–18 min: increase only if able.
 \n   18–20 min: finish hard\, seated.\n6. 14 min Z1 cool-down.\n\nCadenc
 e 80–90 rpm or comfortable natural cadence. Do not force L/R balance. St
 op for calf pain.\nFTP estimate = 0.95 × 20-min average power (not normal
 ized power). Validate in later training. Record 5-min and 20-min power\, H
 R\, cadence\, L/R and RPE.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sub60-2026-w15d7@training.local
DTSTAMP:20261124T161800Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261129
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261130
SUMMARY:W15D7 | Run/Walk 40m + Bike 90m + Swim 2800 yd
DESCRIPTION:W15D7 | Base → Build transition\nPlanned training: 195 min (e
 xcluding extra walking warm-up).\n\nRUN/WALK — 40 min\n5 × (5 min easy 
 run + 3 min walk).\n25 min running\, 15 min walking. Extra walking warm-up
 . Flat route\, RPE 2–3. Do only if recovered from FTP and previous runs.
 \n\nBIKE — 90 min\n10 min Z1 warm-up\n35 min at 60–65% new FTP\n5 min 
 Z1\n30 min at 60–70% new FTP\n10 min Z1 cool-down\nIf no valid FTP\, use
  easy conversational RPE 3–4. Shorten to 60 min or skip if fatigued.\n\n
 SWIM — 2800 yd / 65 min (estimated)\n25 yd pool. Rest after each repeat 
 as listed.\n1. 400 yd easy\; no equipment\; rest 30s.\n2. 2 × 50 yd high-
 elbow catch\; pull buoy\; rest 20s.\n3. 2 × 50 yd catch pressure\; small 
 paddles + pull buoy\; rest 20s.\n4. 2 × 50 yd natural rhythm\; no equipme
 nt\; rest 20s.\n5. 400 yd aerobic RPE 4–5\; no equipment\; rest 30s.\n6.
  400 yd aerobic RPE 4–5\; no equipment\; rest 30s.\n7. 400 yd aerobic RP
 E 4–5\; pull buoy\; rest 30s.\n8. 400 yd aerobic RPE 4–5\; no equipmen
 t\; rest 45s.\n9. 4 × 100 yd aerobic\, CSS + 5–10s/100 yd\, RPE ≤6\; 
 no equipment\; rest 20s.\n10. 100 yd easy cool-down\; no equipment.\nNo fi
 ns or dedicated kicking. If no valid CSS\, use RPE.\n\nCALF CHECK\nDo not 
 run if symptoms persist from the previous session. Stop for local pain. If
  tightness resolves by next day\, do not increase load. Persistent symptom
 s: skip next run. Walking pain or focal bone tenderness: pause running and
  seek sports medicine evaluation.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
